242
00:17:43,221 --> 00:17:45,510
– What is that?
– The elevator feels really stiff, sir.

243
00:17:45,542 --> 00:17:47,362
Right, don't force.

244
00:17:48,336 --> 00:17:52,130
Hi, Margaret, get everybody strapped in,
get everybody strapped in tight.

245
00:17:53,714 --> 00:17:54,661
Ladies and gentlemen-

246
00:17:54,662 --> 00:17:56,374
It's pulling left hard, sir!

247
00:18:04,049 --> 00:18:06,262
Pull it back.
Power back!

248
00:18:06,437 --> 00:18:08,107
<i>SINK RANGE. PULL UP.</i>

249
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:10,122
<i>SINK RANGE. PULL UP.</i>

250
00:18:10,195 --> 00:18:12,770
Ladies and gentlemen,
fasten your seat belts now.

251
00:18:12,778 --> 00:18:15,299
<i>Fasten your seat belts, now!</i>

252
00:18:15,675 --> 00:18:18,276
I have no control on my side.
No control at all, sir.

253
00:18:18,291 --> 00:18:20,984
Lost hydraulics. Center,
this is SouthJet 2-2-7,

254
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:24,423
we've lost our hydraulics and,
feels like our pitch control?

255
00:18:24,454 --> 00:18:26,072
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, Atlanta Center,</i>

256
00:18:26,073 --> 00:18:27,561
- <i>I understand you've lost hydraulics...</i> –
Turn on the back-up pumps, back-up pumps.

257
00:18:27,562 --> 00:18:28,683
- <i>.. and pitch control.</i>
– That is affirmed,

258
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:31,163
we are in a uncontrolled des-

259
00:18:33,286 --> 00:18:36,535
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, Atlanta, say your digits,
are your declaring emergency!?</i>

260
00:18:36,555 --> 00:18:38,045
Everyone is belted in.
Are we going down?

261
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,276
Get belted in, with everybody
in brace position.

262
00:18:40,292 --> 00:18:43,884
Yes, that is affirmed. We are in a dive.
We are in a dive!

263
00:18:43,907 --> 00:18:46,138
We have lost vertical control.

264
00:18:46,157 --> 00:18:48,865
We're gonna need drag. I want you
to throw out everything we got,

265
00:18:48,867 --> 00:18:50,601
the speed brakes, the gear, everything.

266
00:18:50,628 --> 00:18:52,905
Here! Speed brakes!

267
00:18:56,623 --> 00:19:01,488
Brace for descent. Head down, head
forward. Head down, head forward!

268
00:19:01,572 --> 00:19:04,008
Uh, gear's down, I think
hydraulics is the problem, sir.

269
00:19:04,034 --> 00:19:05,879
We need to dump the fuel.

270
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:06,947
Do it!

271
00:19:07,525 --> 00:19:08,925
Ah, alright!

272
00:19:11,746 --> 00:19:15,376
Atlanta Center, this is SouthJet 2-2-7.
We're in an uncontrolled dive.

273
00:19:15,396 --> 00:19:18,877
Descending out of 21,000 feet,
we're declaring an emergency,

274
00:19:19,112 --> 00:19:22,250
we dumped our fuel,
we got a jammed stabilizer or something.

275
00:19:22,271 --> 00:19:24,348
We need a block of altitude
to work the problem,

276
00:19:24,349 --> 00:19:25,958
and a heading to the nearest airport.

277
00:19:26,289 --> 00:19:27,661
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, Hartsfield-Jackson Airport</i>

278
00:19:27,662 --> 00:19:28,349
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, Hartsfield-Jackson Airport</i>
– I can't hold it.

279
00:19:28,364 --> 00:19:29,784
- <i>is 10 O’clock and 20 miles</i>
– Dump the flap, dump the flap.

280
00:19:29,785 --> 00:19:30,341
- <i>is 10 O’clock and 20 miles</i>
– We're still fast!

281
00:19:30,346 --> 00:19:31,919
- <i>from your present position.</i>
– Just do it, do it. 30 degrees!

282
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,737
<i>Turn left heading 3-1-5.</i>

283
00:19:33,909 --> 00:19:35,905
3-1-5, we'll try our best.

284
00:19:35,907 --> 00:19:38,279
Alright, that bought us a little time,
that bought us a little time,

285
00:19:38,294 --> 00:19:40,817
now we got to revert to manual control.
Your side first.

286
00:19:41,165 --> 00:19:42,861
Okay, got it.

287
00:19:43,878 --> 00:19:46,174
Nothing, no control!

288
00:19:46,661 --> 00:19:48,570
Oh no, we're diving again!

289
00:19:48,633 --> 00:19:49,688
<i>PULL UP.</i>

290
00:19:50,044 --> 00:19:51,593
<i>SINK RANGE. PULL UP.</i>

291
00:19:51,646 --> 00:19:53,031
Alright, okay okay.

292
00:19:53,046 --> 00:19:55,485
I can't let go on my side,
see if you can reach my side?

293
00:19:57,024 --> 00:19:58,616
I can't reach it, sir.

294
00:19:58,617 --> 00:20:00,528
Evans don't, stay strapped in,
stay strapped in.

295
00:20:00,544 --> 00:20:02,286
Margaret! Margaret.

296
00:20:07,298 --> 00:20:09,351
Right at 15,000!

297
00:20:09,564 --> 00:20:12,060
Alright, just relax,
calm down, calm down.

298
00:20:12,095 --> 00:20:15,499
Get you strapped into the jump-seat there.
I need you to do something for me.

299
00:20:15,523 --> 00:20:16,348
We're 12-9!

300
00:20:16,364 --> 00:20:19,020
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, Atlanta,
fuel dump is approved.</i>

301
00:20:19,021 --> 00:20:20,128
Thank you.

302
00:20:27,322 --> 00:20:30,290
Cami!
Cami, get back down!

303
00:20:30,322 --> 00:20:32,422
<i>No, Cami, get down!</i>

304
00:20:32,472 --> 00:20:34,674
<i>I see you going below 10,000.
How are you going?</i>

305
00:20:34,682 --> 00:20:35,800
– Uh, not good, not good.

306
00:20:35,801 --> 00:20:36,375
– Uh, not good, not good.
– Oh no!

307
00:20:36,382 --> 00:20:39,381
Margaret, there's a red lever
right here next to my seat.

308
00:20:39,411 --> 00:20:41,033
It says "manual control", you see it?

309
00:20:41,034 --> 00:20:41,690
Uh, yeah.

310
00:20:41,716 --> 00:20:44,596
Okay. On the count at three,
I want you to pull it up,

311
00:20:44,611 --> 00:20:46,546
turn it clockwise, push it back down.

312
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:49,821
Ready?
One, two, three.

313
00:20:52,555 --> 00:20:54,499
That's okay, it's okay.

314
00:20:54,895 --> 00:20:57,147
Aah, come on!

315
00:20:57,838 --> 00:21:00,588
Right, okay.
Okay, it goes up.

316
00:21:01,609 --> 00:21:02,729
Shit!

317
00:21:04,408 --> 00:21:06,682
Cami! Cami!

318
00:21:08,464 --> 00:21:09,628
Margaret!

319
00:21:09,658 --> 00:21:13,546
Oh, Lord. We're coming under 7000,
I see nothing but houses!

320
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,789
Evans, listen to me.

321
00:21:14,816 --> 00:21:17,938
When I say, I want you to retract
the flaps, retract the gears,

322
00:21:17,954 --> 00:21:21,209
trim us nose down, okay, whatever
you think's, gonna be the opposite,

323
00:21:21,233 --> 00:21:23,215
so make sure you trim us nose down.

324
00:21:23,237 --> 00:21:24,496
I trim down, what you gonna do?

325
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:27,129
Margaret. When I tell you,
I want you to push this forward.

326
00:21:27,152 --> 00:21:28,784
Full power, full throttle,
can you do that?

327
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:30,103
– Yeah. Okay.
– Okay. When I tell you.

328
00:21:30,116 --> 00:21:32,103
Wait, wait sir. What do we do,
and why would I trim down?

329
00:21:32,113 --> 00:21:34,649
– We're gonna roll it. Okay?
– What do you mean, rolling?

330
00:21:34,665 --> 00:21:36,282
We gotta do something to stop this dive.

331
00:21:36,283 --> 00:21:38,305
Margaret, what's your son's name?

332
00:21:38,306 --> 00:21:39,022
Trevor.

333
00:21:39,038 --> 00:21:40,348
– Say "I love you, Trevor".
– What?

334
00:21:40,354 --> 00:21:41,711
The black box, say "I love you Trevor".

335
00:21:41,738 --> 00:21:44,778
I love you Trevor, you be a good boy.
Mommy loves you.

336
00:21:44,785 --> 00:21:46,820
Okay, here we go.
I've got control.

337
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:51,054
Oh, Lord Jesus!

338
00:21:53,148 --> 00:21:55,127
– Alright Evans, flaps.
– Flaps!

339
00:21:55,208 --> 00:21:57,054
– Speed brakes.
– Speed brakes!

340
00:22:06,254 --> 00:22:08,621
Margaret. Power!

341
00:22:10,856 --> 00:22:13,185
– Gear up.
– Gear up!

342
00:22:32,751 --> 00:22:34,748
Oh Lord Jesus, we're inverted!

343
00:22:34,764 --> 00:22:37,564
Good flying lesson. We’re level,
we can maintain altitude like this.

344
00:22:37,935 --> 00:22:40,389
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, Atlanta Center,
I see your position</i>

345
00:22:40,392 --> 00:22:42,120
<i>4 and a half miles
southeast of the airport,</i>

346
00:22:42,121 --> 00:22:43,541
<i>descending out of 1,800. Are you OK?</i>

347
00:22:43,593 --> 00:22:46,129
Atlanta Center, this is SouthJet 2-2-7,

348
00:22:46,155 --> 00:22:48,816
we are inverted, I repeat we are inverted.

349
00:22:48,832 --> 00:22:51,345
<i>SoutJet 2-2-7, did you say inverted?</i>

350
00:22:51,358 --> 00:22:53,762
We're losing oil pressure,
pump failure both engines!

351
00:22:53,776 --> 00:22:55,125
We're alright, we're flying.

352
00:23:05,601 --> 00:23:06,713
– Fire in the left engine!

353
00:23:06,714 --> 00:23:08,714
– Fire in the left engine!
– Put it out.

354
00:23:11,121 --> 00:23:13,869
I'm right with you. Look at me,
I'm right with you. Okay?

355
00:23:14,031 --> 00:23:16,698
Atlanta, SouthJet 2-2-7,
where's that airport?

356
00:23:16,731 --> 00:23:19,448
<i>2-2-7, it is one O'clock, three miles.</i>

357
00:23:19,555 --> 00:23:21,984
Alright, we're not gonna make that,
our engines are burning up.

358
00:23:22,064 --> 00:23:25,551
I see a field and a road ahead of us,
we're gonna set it down there.

359
00:23:25,594 --> 00:23:27,002
<i>Roger, 2-2-7.</i>

360
00:23:27,066 --> 00:23:28,610
Oh no, fire in the right, now!

361
00:23:28,627 --> 00:23:30,321
Margaret, we're coming back around.

362
00:23:30,347 --> 00:23:33,709
Margaret, I want you to hit full power,
full throttle, you understand?

363
00:23:33,816 --> 00:23:35,442
Here we go.

364
00:23:35,707 --> 00:23:37,316
Evans, speed brakes.

365
00:23:37,668 --> 00:23:38,937
Speed brakes!

366
00:23:38,974 --> 00:23:41,090
– Flaps full.
– Flaps full.

367
00:23:58,509 --> 00:24:00,079
We're losing the left engine.

368
00:24:00,135 --> 00:24:04,010
<i>SouthJet 2-2-7, I see you descending
through 1000, do you concur?</i>

369
00:24:04,124 --> 00:24:06,226
Margaret, full power.

370
00:24:16,552 --> 00:24:18,026
We lost the left engine!

371
00:24:18,053 --> 00:24:18,901
– Let it go.

372
00:24:18,903 --> 00:24:20,862
– Let it go.
– We're losing power in the right!

373
00:24:23,105 --> 00:24:24,975
We lost all power!

374
00:24:25,093 --> 00:24:26,569
<i>TOO LOW TERRAIN</i>

375
00:24:26,991 --> 00:24:28,366
<i>TOO LOW TERRAIN</i>

376
00:24:28,804 --> 00:24:30,624
<i>TOO LOW TERRAIN</i>

377
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:33,123
Are we gliding?

378
00:24:34,132 --> 00:24:36,592
We're in glide. Pitch for glide.

379
00:24:42,824 --> 00:24:44,824
<i>One hundred.</i>

380
00:24:50,195 --> 00:24:51,411
<i>Fifty.</i>

381
00:24:53,873 --> 00:24:54,993
<i>Forty.</i>

382
00:24:55,294 --> 00:24:56,414
<i>Thirty.</i>

383
00:24:56,901 --> 00:24:57,826
<i>Twenty.</i>

384
00:24:58,014 --> 00:24:59,586
– Brace.
- <i>Ten.</i>

385
00:24:59,798 --> 00:25:01,332
Brace for impact.

386
00:25:16,017 --> 00:25:17,663
I got the pilot.

387
00:25:17,673 --> 00:25:19,967
Somebody, give me a hand here.

388
00:25:20,616 --> 00:25:23,715
Ooh, god, god.

389
00:27:32,454 --> 00:27:34,319
Charlie Anderson?

390
00:27:40,821 --> 00:27:42,600
How you feelin', Whip?

391
00:27:45,011 --> 00:27:48,606
Initial reports look like you pulled
some kind of move up there, man.

392
00:27:48,984 --> 00:27:50,722
You saved a lot of lives.

393
00:27:51,841 --> 00:27:53,241
How many?

394
00:27:54,042 --> 00:27:55,907
On the 102 souls on board,

395
00:27:55,914 --> 00:27:58,903
including the flight crew,
96 of them survived the crash.

396
00:28:01,451 --> 00:28:05,608
Six people died.
Two crew, four passengers.

397
00:28:07,578 --> 00:28:09,808
Who... who on the crew?

398
00:28:14,797 --> 00:28:16,927
– Listen. The protocol is-
– Who in the crew, Charlie?

399
00:28:17,363 --> 00:28:19,529
The protocol is that the NTSB has to be

400
00:28:19,530 --> 00:28:21,646
the first to make contact
with you, I can't...

401
00:28:22,413 --> 00:28:24,879
And their agent's here, so...

402
00:28:25,741 --> 00:28:28,094
Let me go get him, it's a bit of a show.

403
00:28:28,363 --> 00:28:32,069
So there's... half
a dozen of them. Alright.

404
00:28:35,309 --> 00:28:38,119
Hey Craig. Morning.

405
00:28:50,861 --> 00:28:53,590
Captain William Whitaker?

406
00:28:54,086 --> 00:28:56,759
Nod if you can hear me and understand me.

407
00:28:57,279 --> 00:29:00,097
I'm Craig Matson of the NT... NTSB,

408
00:29:00,146 --> 00:29:02,589
and I am required as
the lead on the Go Team

409
00:29:02,597 --> 00:29:04,266
to make initial contact with you,

410
00:29:04,287 --> 00:29:07,391
after a major incident
like the one you had today.

411
00:29:08,657 --> 00:29:11,555
You are in a hospital,
in South Atlanta.

412
00:29:13,600 --> 00:29:17,274
Are you aware that the plane
you were piloting went down?

413
00:29:20,103 --> 00:29:23,101
I have a doctor here who can
explain the medical situation.

414
00:29:24,232 --> 00:29:28,144
I'm Dr. Kenan. And the good news is,
you're in good condition.

415
00:29:28,555 --> 00:29:30,264
You did suffer concussion,

416
00:29:30,351 --> 00:29:32,905
you have numerous lacerations
around your left eye,

417
00:29:32,979 --> 00:29:36,083
we're going to keep the patch on just
for a few days, just as a precaution.

418
00:29:36,109 --> 00:29:38,453
Your eye seems to be okay.

419
00:29:38,537 --> 00:29:40,878
Now the MRI’s show that you
have some strained tendons

420
00:29:40,894 --> 00:29:45,211
in your left knee and ankle,
and you have no broken bones,

421
00:29:45,301 --> 00:29:48,029
but you have some deep bruising
in your left thigh, and some

422
00:29:48,045 --> 00:29:51,375
torn ligaments in your
left wrist. Nothing serious.

423
00:29:51,550 --> 00:29:53,650
So, as soon as we clear your concussion,

424
00:29:53,651 --> 00:29:55,961
and you feel well enough,
you can go home.

425
00:29:56,024 --> 00:30:00,196
That may take a day, maybe three.
Okay?

426
00:30:04,157 --> 00:30:08,195
I won’t ask too much of you
tonight, but as I said,

427
00:30:08,366 --> 00:30:12,154
the NTSB is required
to make initial contact.

428
00:30:13,589 --> 00:30:17,019
How much do you remember about the flight?

429
00:30:19,017 --> 00:30:21,102
Uh, I remember...

430
00:30:23,970 --> 00:30:26,250
I remember everything up to the crash.

431
00:30:26,417 --> 00:30:29,758
Okay... Mr. Whitaker, that’s fine.

432
00:30:30,583 --> 00:30:34,965
I am required to inform you that this
incident did result in the loss of life.

433
00:30:36,846 --> 00:30:42,031
The current information states that
of the 102 souls on board, we lost 6.

434
00:30:42,438 --> 00:30:44,686
Two crew members, and four passengers.

435
00:30:45,231 --> 00:30:47,347
59 people were treated and released.

436
00:30:47,541 --> 00:30:48,719
37 people remain-

437
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,452
– Who died on the crew?

438
00:30:50,777 --> 00:30:56,406
The two flight attendants...
Camelia Satou and Katerina Marquez.

439
00:30:58,762 --> 00:31:02,986
The rep from your Pilot’s Union,
Mr. Anderson, will be our contact for you,

440
00:31:03,002 --> 00:31:07,757
it’s important that you follow your
Union’s guidance on press and media.

441
00:31:08,381 --> 00:31:11,542
The pilot’s union works
closely with the NTSB.

442
00:31:11,844 --> 00:31:16,811
So... I’m gonna head out.
Good luck, Mr. Whitaker.

443
00:31:29,752 --> 00:31:32,789
I knew Trina Marquez, she was...

444
00:31:33,992 --> 00:31:35,851
We spent some time together.

445
00:31:36,102 --> 00:31:38,619
Yeah, apparently she was not strapped in.

446
00:31:39,778 --> 00:31:42,734
Survivor reported
she was assisting a kid.

447
00:31:43,040 --> 00:31:45,595
And Margaret Thomason, how's she doing?

448
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:50,140
Broken collarbone. Just, um, cuts,
I mean she's banged up, but she’s...

449
00:31:50,204 --> 00:31:52,304
she's here too, she's fine.

450
00:31:52,930 --> 00:31:55,841
And Ken Evans, your copilot, he-he...

451
00:31:55,992 --> 00:31:58,227
he took a bad shot to the head.

452
00:31:58,562 --> 00:32:02,096
And now they’re keepin’ him in a coma
just to let the brain swelling go down,

453
00:32:02,114 --> 00:32:05,271
but we feel good about him.
He’s gonna be okay.

454
00:32:08,555 --> 00:32:10,984
What are you doing here, Charlie?

455
00:32:12,212 --> 00:32:13,825
I’m flying a desk now.

456
00:32:14,373 --> 00:32:16,366
I’m a rep for the pilot's Union.

457
00:32:16,783 --> 00:32:18,361
You’re the rep for the pilots’?

458
00:32:18,418 --> 00:32:21,720
Yeah, I'm the one, and when your plane
went down, all the reps got a page

459
00:32:21,730 --> 00:32:25,430
and I just shot up my hand cause
I know you and said I wanted to

460
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:28,110
come and be the first face you’d see.

461
00:32:28,681 --> 00:32:30,358
I'm glad you're here.

462
00:32:30,636 --> 00:32:33,266
The Union's gonna release
a statement on your behalf.

463
00:32:33,626 --> 00:32:36,174
Condolences to the families
who lost their loved ones,

464
00:32:36,225 --> 00:32:39,005
gratitude to the brave men
and women of the flight crew.

465
00:32:39,556 --> 00:32:41,747
That's-you don't have to worry about that.

466
00:32:42,806 --> 00:32:45,311
And I know you and Deana have
been divorced for a while now,

467
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:46,948
but maybe she and your son Will gonna-

468
00:32:47,071 --> 00:32:48,824
Yes, Knuckles...

469
00:32:51,122 --> 00:32:52,854
How old is he now?

470
00:32:52,855 --> 00:32:54,585
Too old. Fifteen.

471
00:32:55,061 --> 00:32:57,190
– Fiteen? Wow.
– Yeah.

472
00:32:58,081 --> 00:33:00,502
When we flew out for Delta,
you were not even married.

473
00:33:01,135 --> 00:33:03,758
We're dinosaurs, Whip.

474
00:33:06,443 --> 00:33:08,901
Do you want me to reach out to Deana?

475
00:33:09,217 --> 00:33:11,887
And see if... she and Will
want to come down or...?

476
00:33:11,910 --> 00:33:13,365
No, I don't want.

477
00:33:13,967 --> 00:33:15,336
