away from any populated areas,

1667
01:58:08,858 --> 01:58:12,996
and allowing him to execute
a forced landing in an open field.

1668
01:58:22,604 --> 01:58:24,992
I heard a loud metallic bang.

1669
01:58:25,883 --> 01:58:27,695
We pitched nose down.

1670
01:58:29,578 --> 01:58:30,513
No control.

1671
01:58:30,576 --> 01:58:34,052
Yeah. First Officer Evans
testimony confirms the same.

1672
01:58:37,094 --> 01:58:38,412
I want to show you something.

1673
01:58:43,207 --> 01:58:45,048
Nothing's happening, uh...

1674
01:58:45,845 --> 01:58:49,312
Its remote control isn't working,
apologies, I can do this manually.

1675
01:59:00,677 --> 01:59:04,120
This is the jackscrew on the
tail assembly that articulates

1676
01:59:04,132 --> 01:59:07,965
the horizontal stabilizer...
also known as the elevator.

1677
01:59:08,337 --> 01:59:12,773
As you can see, the threads on
this screw are almost entirely gone.

1678
01:59:13,346 --> 01:59:19,211
This part was suggested as a maintenance
replacement in January of 2011.

1679
01:59:19,279 --> 01:59:20,839
It was never replaced.

1680
01:59:21,066 --> 01:59:25,141
It had an additional 1200 hours
of flight on it. It finally failed.

1681
01:59:25,514 --> 01:59:30,348
Our investigators have concluded
that the jackscrew snapped

1682
01:59:30,435 --> 01:59:34,175
and the elevator was frozen
in a fixed position,

1683
01:59:34,533 --> 01:59:39,421
locking the elevator in a down position
which forced the plane into a dive.

1684
01:59:39,688 --> 01:59:43,560
The loss of the elevator was,
and I quote our report,

1685
01:59:43,600 --> 01:59:47,277
“a catastrophic event, from
which recovery was improbable

1686
01:59:47,293 --> 01:59:49,730
and stable flight, impossible.”

1687
01:59:53,386 --> 01:59:54,506
Mr. Whitaker...

1688
01:59:55,478 --> 02:00:00,155
I want to talk about the days leading
and the hours leading up to the accident.

1689
02:00:00,346 --> 02:00:03,273
But before I do, I want to
remind you that you are under oath,

1690
02:00:03,282 --> 02:00:06,781
and that any testimony you'll give here
today will be considered admissable

1691
02:00:06,790 --> 02:00:09,514
in any subsequent hearings
or criminal proceedings.

1692
02:00:09,669 --> 02:00:11,834
Do you understand what that means?

1693
02:00:13,875 --> 02:00:17,388
Captain Whitaker, for the record
I need you to verbalize your answer.

1694
02:00:18,405 --> 02:00:20,832
Uh, I'm sorry.
Yes, I understand.

1695
02:00:21,626 --> 02:00:25,405
On the three days leading up
to the accident: Tuesday, October 11th,

1696
02:00:25,422 --> 02:00:28,951
Wednesday, October 12th
or Thursday, October 13th,

1697
02:00:28,961 --> 02:00:33,211
did you consume any alcohol
or other intoxicating elements?

1698
02:00:34,272 --> 02:00:35,636
No, I did not.

1699
02:00:35,956 --> 02:00:39,813
On the morning of the accident,
Friday, October 14th,

1700
02:00:39,962 --> 02:00:45,221
did you consume any alcohol,
or ingest any chemicals or drugs

1701
02:00:45,222 --> 02:00:48,784
that may have impaired your
ability to perform your job?

1702
02:00:49,417 --> 02:00:50,887
No, I did not.

1703
02:00:51,964 --> 02:00:56,134
Mr. Whitaker, do you now or
have you ever had a problem

1704
02:00:56,136 --> 02:01:00,343
with alcohol dependency,
alcoholism or drug addiction?

1705
02:01:00,510 --> 02:01:01,680
No.

1706
02:01:04,004 --> 02:01:06,517
Okay, Mr. Whitaker, we’re about done.

1707
02:01:13,346 --> 02:01:18,044
Due to the severe turbulence in the
early part of the flight, you asked

1708
02:01:18,045 --> 02:01:21,584
the flight crew to suspend the beverage
service on the plane, is that correct?

1709
02:01:21,833 --> 02:01:25,397
Yes, That's correct, I suspended
the drink service on the plane.

1710
02:01:25,446 --> 02:01:30,193
Are you aware that our investigators
found two single-service vodka bottles

1711
02:01:30,194 --> 02:01:31,642
in the galley trash bin?

1712
02:01:34,156 --> 02:01:36,083
Yeah, I'm aware of that.

1713
02:01:36,730 --> 02:01:39,141
There were five crew members on board

1714
02:01:39,149 --> 02:01:41,782
that who would have had access
to the beverage trolley.

1715
02:01:42,116 --> 02:01:44,087
Less than an hour after the accident,

1716
02:01:44,095 --> 02:01:47,176
blood was taken from each
of these crew members, yourself,

1717
02:01:47,672 --> 02:01:52,279
first officer Evans, flight
attendant Margaret Thomason...

1718
02:01:52,676 --> 02:01:58,072
and posthumously from Camelia
Satou, and Katerina Marquez.

1719
02:01:59,215 --> 02:02:02,433
A toxicology analysis was performed and...

1720
02:02:03,121 --> 02:02:05,218
three of these tests came back negative,

1721
02:02:05,219 --> 02:02:09,286
one was disqualified for
technical reasons, and one...

1722
02:02:09,790 --> 02:02:14,819
tested positive for alcohol.
It registered a .17 blood alcohol level.

1723
02:02:14,820 --> 02:02:16,317
Are you aware of that?

1724
02:02:17,337 --> 02:02:19,227
Yeah. I'm aware of it now.

1725
02:02:25,977 --> 02:02:30,068
Miss Marquez was not only a colleague,
but you knew her outside of work,

1726
02:02:30,076 --> 02:02:32,150
is that correct?

1727
02:02:33,153 --> 02:02:34,833
Outside of work...

1728
02:02:35,755 --> 02:02:37,036
No, not really.

1729
02:02:37,148 --> 02:02:39,814
Did you know Miss Marquez
had a drinking problem?

1730
02:02:40,917 --> 02:02:42,130
No, I did not.

1731
02:02:42,239 --> 02:02:44,564
Did you ever see her drink to excess?

1732
02:02:47,083 --> 02:02:48,549
No, I did not.

1733
02:02:48,599 --> 02:02:51,503
Were you aware that she was
twice treated for alcohol addiction,

1734
02:02:51,507 --> 02:02:55,536
the last time was 16 months ago
and paid for by SouthJet Airlines?

1735
02:02:56,992 --> 02:02:58,392
No, I did not.

1736
02:03:08,759 --> 02:03:15,319
Is it your opinion... that Katerina
Marquez... drank on that flight?

1737
02:03:26,930 --> 02:03:28,725
Could you repeat the question?

1738
02:03:29,479 --> 02:03:34,039
Is it your opinion that Katerina
Marquez drank on that flight?

1739
02:03:46,132 --> 02:03:47,415
I’m sorry. My what?

1740
02:03:47,548 --> 02:03:48,668
Your opinion, Captain.

1741
02:03:48,899 --> 02:03:52,131
Since her toxicology report
is the only toxicology report

1742
02:03:52,143 --> 02:03:56,669
that is admissable in this hearing, and
she in fact tested positive for alcohol,

1743
02:03:56,670 --> 02:04:00,574
is it your opinion that Katerina Marquez

1744
02:04:00,595 --> 02:04:04,299
drank those 2 bottles
of vodka on the plane?

1745
02:04:15,850 --> 02:04:19,066
I’m sorry Mr. Whitaker, I couldn’t
hear you. What did you say?

1746
02:04:21,878 --> 02:04:23,844
I said, "God, help me."

1747
02:04:24,615 --> 02:04:27,464
Yes, well. However, is it your opinion-

1748
02:04:27,475 --> 02:04:28,909
It's my opinion...

1749
02:04:29,168 --> 02:04:30,988
Trina did not...

1750
02:04:31,339 --> 02:04:32,891
drink that Vodka.

1751
02:04:33,560 --> 02:04:34,813
Excuse me, Mr. Whitaker?

1752
02:04:34,829 --> 02:04:36,399
She saved the boy’s life, that's-

1753
02:04:36,400 --> 02:04:38,113
Could you speak louder, Captain Whitaker?

1754
02:04:38,121 --> 02:04:40,662
Trina Marquez did not drink the vodka.

1755
02:04:42,247 --> 02:04:44,354
Because I drank the vodka.

1756
02:04:47,333 --> 02:04:48,510
Objection!

1757
02:04:49,422 --> 02:04:51,338
Please be seated sir. This-

1758
02:04:52,268 --> 02:04:53,388
Sir.

1759
02:04:53,539 --> 02:04:54,416
– I drank the vodka bottles-

1760
02:04:54,417 --> 02:04:56,013
– I drank the vodka bottles-
– Did you hear what I said, I object!

1761
02:04:56,021 --> 02:04:58,544
Please be seated sir,
this is not a court room.

1762
02:04:58,614 --> 02:05:00,064
Well, I object anyway!

1763
02:05:01,550 --> 02:05:03,829
I drank the vodka bottles on the plane.

1764
02:05:05,730 --> 02:05:10,377
Captain Whitaker. On the three nights
before the accident, October 11-

1765
02:05:10,388 --> 02:05:15,479
October 11, October 12 and 13th
and 14th, I was intoxicated.

1766
02:05:15,490 --> 02:05:18,472
I drank all of those days, I drank...

1767
02:05:19,082 --> 02:05:20,482
in excess.

1768
02:05:21,912 --> 02:05:24,784
– On the morning of the accident-
– I was drunk.

1769
02:05:32,846 --> 02:05:34,297
I'm drunk now.

1770
02:05:40,832 --> 02:05:42,557
I'm drunk right now...

1771
02:05:43,191 --> 02:05:44,714
Miss Block...

1772
02:05:51,621 --> 02:05:53,306
because I'm alcoholic.

1773
02:06:19,191 --> 02:06:20,625
That was it.

1774
02:06:24,261 --> 02:06:25,743
I was finished.

1775
02:06:27,703 --> 02:06:29,138
I was done.

1776
02:06:32,130 --> 02:06:37,870
It was as if I had reached
my life long limit... for lies.

1777
02:06:39,153 --> 02:06:42,159
I could not tell one more lie.

1778
02:06:45,685 --> 02:06:47,409
And maybe I'm a sucker.

1779
02:06:49,496 --> 02:06:51,946
Because if I had told just one more lie,

1780
02:06:52,436 --> 02:06:55,001
I could have walked away
from all that mess...

1781
02:06:55,710 --> 02:06:59,289
kept my wings, kept my
false sense of pride...

1782
02:07:01,933 --> 02:07:06,821
and most importantly, I could have avoided
being locked up in here with all of you,

1783
02:07:07,543 --> 02:07:10,415
nice folks for the last 13 months.

1784
02:07:14,030 --> 02:07:15,535
But I'm here.

1785
02:07:16,525 --> 02:07:18,525
And I'll be here for at least the...

1786
02:07:19,205 --> 02:07:21,757
next four or five years.
And that's fair.

1787
02:07:25,638 --> 02:07:28,542
I betrayed the public trust. I did.

1788
02:07:28,732 --> 02:07:32,916
That’s what the judge explained to me.
I had betrayed the public trust.

1789
02:07:34,704 --> 02:07:37,843
The FAA, they took away
my pilot's license.

1790
02:07:39,813 --> 02:07:41,100
And that's fair.

1791
02:07:42,073 --> 02:07:45,664
My chances of ever flying
again are slim to none.

1792
02:07:47,703 --> 02:07:49,349
And I accept that.

1793
02:07:52,174 --> 02:07:55,242
I got a lot of time to think
about it, the all of it.

1794
02:07:57,903 --> 02:07:59,119
Doing some writing.

1795
02:08:01,088 --> 02:08:05,121
I wrote letters to each of the
families that had lost loved ones.

1796
02:08:08,363 --> 02:08:10,384
Some of ‘em were able
to hear my apology...

1797
02:08:12,582 --> 02:08:14,032
some of ‘em never will.

1798
02:08:15,866 --> 02:08:18,395
I also apologized to...

1799
02:08:19,606 --> 02:08:24,135
all the people that tried to help me...
along the way, but I...

1800
02:08:25,814 --> 02:08:28,468
couldn't or wouldn't listen.

1801
02:08:31,776 --> 02:08:33,664
People like my wife...

1802
02:08:37,401 --> 02:08:39,062
My ex-wife...

1803
02:08:43,452 --> 02:08:44,942
My son.

1804
02:08:48,237 --> 02:08:51,345
And again like I said, you know,
some of them will...

1805
02:08:53,758 --> 02:08:56,287
never forgive me, some of them won't...

1806
02:08:58,726 --> 02:09:00,606
But at least I'm sober.

1807
02:09:03,224 --> 02:09:06,480
I thank God for that,
I’m grateful for that.

1808
02:09:09,307 --> 02:09:11,211
And this is gonna sound really stupid

1809
02:09:11,212 --> 02:09:13,843
coming from a man who’s
locked up in prison...

1810
02:09:16,255 --> 02:09:18,393
but for the first time in my life...

1811
02:09:19,903 --> 02:09:21,456
I’m free.

1812
02:09:34,995 --> 02:09:37,782
Whitaker.
You got a visitor.

1813
02:10:15,256 --> 02:10:17,587
– You have 40 minutes.
– Okay.

1814
02:10:28,059 --> 02:10:29,858
Look at you, boy.

1815
02:10:30,460 --> 02:10:31,666
How you doing?

1816
02:10:31,989 --> 02:10:33,541
– Good.
– You look good.

1817
02:10:34,847 --> 02:10:36,673
Com'on, sit down.

1818
02:10:38,343 --> 02:10:41,299
This is a surprise.
Did you get that gift I sent you?

1819
02:10:41,309 --> 02:10:41,970
– Yeah.
– Yeah?

1820
02:10:41,986 --> 02:10:43,259
– Yeah, I got it.
– You like it?

1821
02:10:43,260 --> 02:10:44,380
– Yeah.
– Good...

1822
02:10:46,829 --> 02:10:49,945
– How's your mom?
– Fine. She's alright.

1823
02:10:51,711 --> 02:10:55,576
My College counselor wanted
me to come in... interview you.

1824
02:10:56,631 --> 02:10:57,646
Me?

1825
02:10:57,832 --> 02:11:01,142
Yeah. I'm writing essays
for College applications.

1826
02:11:01,205 --> 02:11:02,325
Good.

1827
02:11:02,651 --> 02:11:04,117
I need your help.

1828
02:11:04,430 --> 02:11:05,830
So you got it.

1829
02:11:07,076 --> 02:11:11,919
And then... this essay.
The essay that I have to write...

1830
02:11:13,721 --> 02:11:20,156
it's called... “the most fascinating
person... that I’ve never met.”

1831
02:11:30,927 --> 02:11:32,605
So...

1832
02:11:37,169 --> 02:11:38,636
Who are you?

1833
02:11:47,743 --> 02:11:49,280
That's a good question.

1834
02:11:54,353 --> 02:11:59,623
Transcript and sync: jcdr
